This example vendors and adapts model code from:

  OpenGVLab/VideoMAEv2  (https://github.com/OpenGVLab/VideoMAEv2)
  and the HuggingFace checkpoint OpenGVLab/VideoMAEv2-Base
  Paper: "VideoMAE V2: Scaling Video Masked Autoencoders with Dual Masking",
         Wang et al., CVPR 2023.

The VideoMAEv2-Base pretrained weights are distributed by OpenGVLab under
CC-BY-NC-4.0 (non-commercial). Those weights are NOT redistributed here; they are
downloaded at runtime from HuggingFace by src/download_vmae2.py. The vendored
modeling code is based on BEiT / timm / DeiT / DINO codebases as noted in the
upstream files.
